        "prerequisite": "Point Blank Shot, Precise Shot.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "rules": {
          "benefit": "When a target is within 10 feet of a solid, reasonably smooth surface, you may ricochet a ranged attack from that surface and ignore the target's cover bonus to AC. The attack takes a -2 penalty on both its attack and damage rolls. An imperfect surface may still be usable at the GM's discretion. You may attempt this against full cover by guessing the target's location, but the target still has total concealment. A character proficient with a moonglaive ignores Trick Shot's attack and damage penalties when using one.",
