    "description": {
      "chat": "",
      "unidentified": "",
      "value": "<p><strong>Category:</strong> General feat</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Point Blank Shot, Precise Shot.</p><p><strong>Summary:</strong> Ricochet a ranged attack from a solid surface to bypass cover at -2 attack and damage.</p><p><strong>Benefit:</strong> When a target is within 10 feet of a solid, reasonably smooth surface, you may ricochet a ranged attack from that surface and ignore the target&#39;s cover bonus to AC. The attack takes a -2 penalty on both its attack and damage rolls. An imperfect surface may still be usable at the GM&#39;s discretion. You may attempt this against full cover by guessing the target&#39;s location, but the target still has total concealment. A character proficient with a moonglaive ignores Trick Shot&#39;s attack and damage penalties when using one.</p><p><strong>Warrior bonus feat:</strong> Yes</p><p><strong>Foundry and GM handling:</strong> The GM adjudicates geometry and surface quality; apply cover, concealment, moonglaive, attack, and damage adjustments manually.</p>"
    },
